Message-ID: <200802051728.m15HSXpg002428@smtp.washington.edu>

In S+FinMetrics there are functions (eg. unitroot, stationaryTest) for
testing the hypothesis that a time series is integrated of order 1 (unit
root non-stationary - y(t) = y(t-1) + u(t), u(t) ~ I(0)) against the
alternative that the series is integrated of order zero (e.g. covariance
stationary)  and vice-versa. However, this is just a test for a very
particular type of non-stationarity. 

