Hello Sebastien,

 

 

par(oma=c(3,6,1,2),xpd=T) # xpd to be able to plot outside the plot
region and oma to change the                       #
spaces of the margins

xyplot(b~a|ID, 

     data=mydf, 

     panel=function(x,y,subscripts){ 

       panel.xyplot(x, y, pch=16) 

       panel.xyplot(mydf$a[subscripts],mydf$c[subscripts],pch=3) 

       }, 

       as.table=T, 

       subscripts=T, 

       key = list(space="bottom", x=0.5,y=-0.2,

       transparent = T, 

       text=list(c("b", "c")), 

       lines = list(pch = c(16,3), type = c("p", "p"))), 

     ) 

You can have it on the "top" side without any overlap.

 

Hope this helps,

 

Thank you,

 

Samer

