Sorry Jenny,



The snippet I gave you came from a R code I wrote some time ago. The
interaction functions are somehow different in R and Splus... So, here
is how you could
split your particular data.frame. 



split.factor<-interaction(data[,c(1,2)])

mydf.split <- split(mydf,split.factor)



Note that interaction in Splus puts a
dot between the different element used to builds each value of its
output. This is a potential problem if you want to post-process the
names of your split data.set, since the dot sign is fairly commonly
used (e.g. in numbers!!!).



