I'm working with some models and I want to investigate all, say, three 
term models, give a choice of 8 total terms. Then I want to examine all 
four term models, given a choice or 8 terms, etc. Assume all of my data 
are in a 9 column data frame: one column for the response, and 8 columns 
of predictors.

I can use combinations() to give me the column numbers, but I can't 
figure out how to build a valid formula given the column number. For 
example, I need a formula that looks like, say:

observation ~ R + Z + uvel

where R is the name of column 4, Z is the name of column 5, and uvel is 
the name of column 7 in my 9 column data frame.

I'd like to construct this formula from the vector c(4,5,7). So, when I 
hand my formula-generating function c(4,5,7) it generates a formula 
class object that is observation ~ R + Z + uvel.

How might I do this?

Kim Elmore

