From lawrence-hunsicker at uiowa.edu  Fri Nov  6 15:46:32 2009
From: lawrence-hunsicker at uiowa.edu (Hunsicker, Lawrence)
Date: Fri, 06 Nov 2009 09:46:32 -0600
Subject: Help with lapply
Message-ID: <2B80F69A8A189D48B0E668B0BBC6BA42045DFC12@HC-MAIL13.healthcare.uiowa.edu>

Good morning folks:

I need help in using lapply correctly.  Consider the following three
calls:

lapply(c(1:2, 4:6),
       function (x) {
         c(names(temp)[x], summary(temp[[x]]))
    })
   
lapply(c(1:2, 4:6),
       function (x) {
        temp1 <-summary(lm(ckdepi6mo ~ temp[[1]], data=temp))
        c(names(temp)[x], 1 - pf(temp1$fstatistic[1],
temp1$fstatistic[2], temp1$fstatistic[3]))
    })

lapply(c(1:2, 4:6),
       function (x) {
        temp1 <-summary(lm(ckdepi6mo ~ temp[[x]], data=temp))
        c(names(temp)[x], 1 - pf(temp1$fstatistic[1],
temp1$fstatistic[2], temp1$fstatistic[3]))
    })
   
The first call works the way that I would expect, returning a list with
the name of the column in temp and its summary.

The second call works the way that I would expect, returning a list with
the name of the column in temp and the p value of the F-test for the lm
call on column 1 (repeated for each column name).

But the third call abends with the message:

Problem in FUN(...X.sub.i....): Object "x" not found
Use traceback() to see the call stack

What do I have to do to make "x" visible to lm in the third call above?
The "x" is visible to the call to summary in the first call, and
temp[[1]] does return the first column of temp properly for the call to
lm.  But lm seems not to be able to find "x" in the third call.

I'm stumped.

Thanks in advance to any help that any of you can give me.

Larry Hunsicker

