Yiwu, 
  The arguments to the function that is to be integrated must have all of the arguments supplied in the call to integrate. Check out the revised code below. Note that I had to change the argument k to kk in the integrand function because there is an argument to integrate that begins with k, but not kk. 
  I also changed your print calls to see all of the values passed. 
Dave 


Yield.recruit<-function(Linf=Linf,k=k,t0=t0,cc=cc,ts=ts,Fi=Fi,M=M,tc=tc,tr=tr,tm=tm,a=a,b=b) 

{ 

integrand<-function(x,Linf=Linf,kk=k,t0=t0,cc=cc,ts=ts,Fi=Fi,M=M,tc=tc,tr=tr,tm=tm,a=a,b=b) 

{print(match.call()) 

Fi*exp(-M*(tc-tr))*exp(-(Fi+M)*(x-tc))*a*(Linf*(1-exp(-kk*(x/12-.04167-t0+cc/2/pi*sin(2*pi*(x/12-.04167-ts))))))^b 

} 

integrate(integrand,lower=tc,upper=tm, Linf=Linf,kk=k,t0=t0,cc=cc,ts=ts,Fi=Fi,M=M,tc=tc,tr=tr,tm=tm,a=a,b=b)$integral 

} 

  

Yield.recruit(Linf=36.57,k=1.64,t0=-0.15,cc=0.22,ts=-0.3,Fi=.2,M=0.184,tr=6,tc=6,tm=24,a=0.00368,b=2.57) 





