Terry:

Your comments are:

	a) humorous,
	b) to the point and accurate, and
	c) very informative.

Thanks, Terry.  My sense is that I can still afford my S-Plus license,
but, like you, I will be honing my R skills against the day that I
finally have to complete the switch to R.  

It's really the easy graphics that keeps me in S-Plus.  I think that I
can handle the workspace issue well enough.  It wouldn't be necessary
for Tibco to incorporate all of the new stuff in R all the time, and I
agree that they couldn't afford to do so at a price that we users could
afford.  But it would be really nice to be able to edit graphics
interactively the way that one can in S-Plus but not in R (so far as I
understand).  Maybe if TIBCO made it a bit easier to import R routines
into S-Plus -- which they should be able to do, since they have figured
out how to use R routines, along with S-Plus, in Spotfire -- we could do
our statistics with R programs and then use S-Plus for the graphics.
All TIBCO would have to do, then, is to maintain the ability to use R
objects as the basis for S-PLUS graphics routines.

But then, maybe I don't understand.

Larry Hunsicker



