I must chime in that I've been concerned over this as well. As a 
research meteorologist, I find the S-Plus object-oriented graphics well 
worth the license fee. That, and the fact that the S-Plus resample 
library is so self consistent and well harmonized. I have (so far) found 
R's resample capability less pleasant to use, and the last time I 
looked, some of the functionality within S-Plus's resample does not 
exist within R.

As Larry wrote, I'll continue to pay the license fee simply because I 
have a fair bit invested in S code that I've written such that it plays 
well with all the other S stuff. But, like apparently everyone else, I 
can't ignore the writing on the wall: S-Plus as we know it is slowly on 
its way out.

Kim Elmore

