Bob,

Two other suggestions:

1) Visit www.kdnuggets.com and look through the archives. Gregory conducts a
number of similar surveys all the time. R (along with many of the others) is
included in his tools and software surveys. The audience is admittedly data
mining biased, but a lot of overlap nonetheless.

2) Look at the number of jobs posted that list stats packages as a preferred
or required skill over time. I was confronted a few years ago with a similar
task and for expedience I had my HR recruiter run some queries against her
online databases to measure the number of hits for R. Demand for specific
skills is a compelling metric.

Cheers,
Greg James



