Subject: Re: Johnson's skewness adjusted t-test
Message-ID: <4C65079A.5311.9E183A@r.verwer.nin.knaw.nl>

Dear all,

Thanks to Kim Elmore for asking an interesting question and Tim 
Hesterberg for his answers. When I skimmed quickly over the 
paper by NJ Johnson (full reference: Modified t-tests and 
confidence intervals for asymmetrical populations. JASA 72 (1978) 
536-544) I wrongly guessed that it needed a jackknife. For those 
interested: the (1-a) percent confidence interval as indicated 
already by Tim only needs the skewness:
(mean(x) + skewness/(6*var*N)) +/- (t(a/2,df)*stdev/sqrt(N)).


Kind regards,

Ronald





