I am having some strange results when I did an exercise for propensity score simulation. As far as I know based on literatures, adjusting the propensity as a covariate in an observational study setting can reduce the bias in the estimates of exposure/treatment. However, I got quite opposite results. 

My simulation code in R/S-plus:

nsim<-3000

model1.grp.coeff<-as.numeric(nsim)
model1.grp.pval<-as.numeric(nsim)
