That should be logit(prop.score) (if fitted.values are fitted 
probabilities)

You neglected to put the covariates in the model, so your model is 
misspecified.  Using propensity score does not mean that you don't 
need to adjust for outcome heterogeneity.

Your example is not very realistic.  In general a propensity analysis 
might consider 20-100 covariates when you pre-specify the known 
important covariates to put into the model (say 5-10 of them) and add 
in logit propensity and some nonlinear transformations of it (say 
using splines) based on all measured baseline covariates.

