From phlasky at earthlink.net  Fri Aug 13 14:58:11 2010
From: phlasky at earthlink.net (Paul H. Lasky)
Date: Fri, 13 Aug 2010 07:58:11 -0700
Subject: Skewness and Kurtosis Adjusted t Tests
Message-ID: <13343742.1281711491498.JavaMail.root@elwamui-chisos.atl.sa.earthlink.net>


 In the hedge fund world portfolio managers routinely  adjust t with:

 tadj = t*[ 1 + t*Skew/6 - t^2*(Kurt-3)/24 ] ,

   where Skew is the sample Skewness and Kurt the sample Kurtosis. Notice that for left skew and  playkurtic distributions ( peaked distribution with fat tails, Kurt > 3), tadj is smaller.

  Paul H. Lasky
  B & P Consultants
  San Diego, California 

 
