Hello,

yes Bill, this is exactly what I was after.  I also got a solution by
interchanging the data.frames in the call to "match.data.frame".  Following
you will find a resources comparaison on a real world data set.

ttt <- GeoBD.all[, c(37:160, 204)]
dim(ttt)
[1] 208327    125
resources({ttt.na <- as.data.frame(is.na(ttt))
           ttt.unique <- unique.data.frame(ttt.na)
           ttt.unique <- ttt.unique[rowSums(ttt.unique) > 0, ] ## To
                  ## differentiate rows with no missing and rows with one
missing
           ttt.ind <- match.data.frame(x = ttt.na, table = ttt.unique)
           ttt.ind.list <- lapply(seq(1, nrow(ttt.unique)), FUN =
function(i, ind)
                                  which(ind == i), ind = ttt.ind)
          })
