Message-ID: <77EB52C6DD32BA4D87471DCD70C8D700038B1A8B@NA-PA-VBE03.na.tibco.com>

After running
  dob <- "11/04/1949"
  today <- "10/13/2010"
  age <- timeDate(today) - timeDate(dob)
age is a timeSpan object and help(class.timeSpan) tells
about that class.  One way is to set its format slot
to your favorite format.  E.g.,
  age@format <- "%y years + %D days"
results in age printing as
  60 years + 358 days

If you set options("tspan.out.format") before making
the age object then it will put that into its format
slot.


