	All, 
	  That sounds like a very appealing way to compute age, but
timeSpan does not know about leap years. Take this as an example: 
	> timeDate('03/01/2000') - timeDate('03/01/1964') -> DT 
	> DT@format <- "%y years + %D days" 
	> DT 
	[1] 36 years + 9 days 
	   This would clearly result in reporting the wrong age in some
cases. Note that Walt would be 61 on 10/20/2010! 
	  I do not have a function for computing age, but the age can be
computed by using mdy to compute the month day and year of each date.
Then compute the differences, call them yd, md, and dd. 
	If md is > 0, then the age is yd, 
	else if md == 0 and dd > 0, then age is yd, 
	otherwise age is yd - 1 
	Dave 
	
	
	
	
	
