Message-ID: <20101015173802.GB12940@seadevintranet01.na.tibco.com>

On Fri, Oct 15, 2010 at 10:13:10AM +0100, Patrick Burns wrote:
> I have an R package, don't have S+, and I want to make the
> functionality of the R package as conveniently available to S+ users
> as possible.
> 
> What's the best way to do that?
> 
> A hard part seems to be getting the html versions of help files, which
> to my eye appear in R by magic.

The S+ package system uses Rd files as the source format for help files.
When the package is installed under Unix/Linux the Rd files are
converted (magically) to html. On Windows the Rd files are all converted
into a Windows CHM file.

If you submit your package to CSAN (the S+ package repository), a binary
version of the package for Windows will be made available along with the
source version. To submit a package to CSAN, send the source archive
(.zip or .tar.gz) via email to: s-packages at tibco.com

More information about packages under S-PLUS is available in the
Guide to Packages.  The latest version can be found here:

    http://csan.insightful.com/doc/spluspackages.pdf

-Stephen
