Subject: Answer to timeDate query
Message-ID: <4CC7372D.1020806@noaa.gov>

Thanks to Eric Zivot for steering me in the right direction.

My problem was that I had times rescorded with the wrong time zone and I 
could not change the time zone without changing the displayed values. in 
my example, times and dates are for the Central time zone, but I needed 
times and dates in UTC. Unfortunatley, the "time.zone" slot of the 
timeDate already had UTC in it. WHenever I tried to change it to CST, 
the displayed value showed a shift of -6 h. WHat I really wanted to do 
was simply add 6 h to all the times, with the dates automatically 
adjusted as needed.

Eric introduced me to the timeRelative object and all is now as it needs 
to be.

